      "writing": {
        "prompt": "Explain why eight bits cannot store every whole-number reading from 0 to 300, and justify the minimum width.",
        "model": "Eight unsigned bits give 256 patterns, representing 0–255. Since 300 exceeds 255, eight bits are insufficient. Nine bits represent 0–511, so nine bits are sufficient and are the minimum.",
